From be05dc19cb147218faa2e7102fbc036081981b80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:55:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 50/52] CUDA/HIP: LFM2 shortconv: b*x and c*conv folded into
 the fused SSM_CONV, which writes the q8_1 out_proj input (GGML_HIP_CONV_MUL)

The LFM2 shortconv block ran in_proj -> MUL(b, x) -> fused SSM_CONV -> MUL(c, conv) ->
quantize_q8_1 -> out_proj. The fused conv plan now also folds the input MUL (it reads b
and x from the in_proj output and multiplies them, the MUL node is elided) and the output
MUL right after the SSM_CONV (it writes that node, gate * conv), and the kernel writes the
q8_1 copy of the result for the out_proj MMVQ (producer path, DPP exchanges, same bits as
quantize_q8_1). Same products as the MUL kernels; both MULs or none; the folded MULs'
operands and outputs are checked for overlaps with every other input. GDN (Qwen) conv
launches are unchanged (template flag).

LFM2.5-24B-A2B decode: 682 -> 595 kernels/token (3 per shortconv layer).
llama-bench tg128 -r 5, 3 interleaved rounds, same binary env off/on:
4.979 -> 4.800 ms/token (200.9 -> 208.3 t/s). Greedy md5 equal (LFM plain, Qwen plain +
MTP); test-backend-ops SSM_CONV, MUL, RMS_NORM pass.
